{"declarations":[{"header":"<div class=\"decl_header\"><span class=\"decl_kind\">def</span><span class=\"decl_name\"> <a class=\"break_within\" href=\"./Std/Async/Watchdog.html#Std.Async.Watchdog.hasFired\"><span class=\"name\">Std</span>.<span class=\"name\">Async</span>.<span class=\"name\">Watchdog</span>.<span class=\"name\">hasFired</span></a> </span><span class=\"decl_args\"><span class=\"fn\">(<span class=\"fn\">wd</span> : <a href=\"./Std/Async/Watchdog.html#Std.Async.Watchdog\">Watchdog</a>)</span></span> <span class=\"decl_args\"> :</span><div class=\"decl_type\"><span class=\"fn\"><a href=\"./Init/System/IO.html#BaseIO\">BaseIO</a> <a href=\"./Init/Prelude.html#Bool\">Bool</a></span></div></div>","info":{"doc":"Returns `true` if a wait outlived its deadline and its context was cancelled with `.deadline`. If\nthe watchdog has marked a wait as late but not cancelled the context yet, this cancels it first.","docLink":"./Std/Async/Watchdog.html#Std.Async.Watchdog.hasFired","kind":"def","line":221,"name":"Std.Async.Watchdog.hasFired","sourceLink":"https://github.com/leanprover/lean4/blob/0b77e12952ad39077d80d8bd6b66d601f225c321/src/Std/Async/Watchdog.lean#L221-L226"}},{"header":"<div class=\"decl_header\"><span class=\"decl_kind\">def</span><span class=\"decl_name\"> <a class=\"break_within\" href=\"./Std/Async/Watchdog.html#Std.Async.Watchdog.disarm\"><span class=\"name\">Std</span>.<span class=\"name\">Async</span>.<span class=\"name\">Watchdog</span>.<span class=\"name\">disarm</span></a> </span><span class=\"decl_args\"><span class=\"fn\">(<span class=\"fn\">wd</span> : <a href=\"./Std/Async/Watchdog.html#Std.Async.Watchdog\">Watchdog</a>)</span></span> <span class=\"decl_args\"> :</span><div class=\"decl_type\"><span class=\"fn\"><a href=\"./Init/System/IO.html#BaseIO\">BaseIO</a> <a href=\"./Init/Prelude.html#Bool\">Bool</a></span></div></div>","info":{"doc":"Ends the current wait. Returns `true` if a wait outlived its deadline, in which case the context is\ncancelled with `.deadline`. A wait whose context was cancelled for another reason first is not\nreported.","docLink":"./Std/Async/Watchdog.html#Std.Async.Watchdog.disarm","kind":"def","line":203,"name":"Std.Async.Watchdog.disarm","sourceLink":"https://github.com/leanprover/lean4/blob/0b77e12952ad39077d80d8bd6b66d601f225c321/src/Std/Async/Watchdog.lean#L203-L219"}},{"header":"<div class=\"decl_header\"><span class=\"decl_kind\">def</span><span class=\"decl_name\"> <a class=\"break_within\" href=\"./Std/Async/Watchdog.html#Std.Async.Watchdog.arm\"><span class=\"name\">Std</span>.<span class=\"name\">Async</span>.<span class=\"name\">Watchdog</span>.<span class=\"name\">arm</span></a> </span><span class=\"decl_args\"><span class=\"fn\">(<span class=\"fn\">wd</span> : <a href=\"./Std/Async/Watchdog.html#Std.Async.Watchdog\">Watchdog</a>)</span></span> <span class=\"decl_args\"><span class=\"fn\">(<span class=\"fn\">timeout</span> : <a href=\"./Std/Time/Time/Unit/Millisecond.html#Std.Time.Millisecond.Offset\">Time.Millisecond.Offset</a>)</span></span> <span class=\"decl_args\"> :</span><div class=\"decl_type\"><span class=\"fn\"><a href=\"./Init/System/IO.html#BaseIO\">BaseIO</a> <a href=\"./Init/Prelude.html#Unit\">Unit</a></span></div></div>","info":{"doc":"Starts a wait that must end within `timeout`. Arming again before `disarm` replaces the deadline.\nDoes nothing once the watchdog has fired.","docLink":"./Std/Async/Watchdog.html#Std.Async.Watchdog.arm","kind":"def","line":187,"name":"Std.Async.Watchdog.arm","sourceLink":"https://github.com/leanprover/lean4/blob/0b77e12952ad39077d80d8bd6b66d601f225c321/src/Std/Async/Watchdog.lean#L187-L192"}},{"header":"<div class=\"decl_header\"><span class=\"decl_kind\">def</span><span class=\"decl_name\"> <a class=\"break_within\" href=\"./Std/Async/Watchdog.html#Std.Async.Watchdog.armAfter\"><span class=\"name\">Std</span>.<span class=\"name\">Async</span>.<span class=\"name\">Watchdog</span>.<span class=\"name\">armAfter</span></a> </span><span class=\"impl_arg\"><span class=\"decl_args\"><span class=\"fn\">{<span class=\"fn\">α</span> : <a href=\"./foundational_types.html\">Type</a> u_1}</span></span> </span><span class=\"decl_args\"><span class=\"fn\">(<span class=\"fn\">wd</span> : <a href=\"./Std/Async/Watchdog.html#Std.Async.Watchdog\">Watchdog</a>)</span></span> <span class=\"decl_args\"><span class=\"fn\">(<span class=\"fn\">task</span> : <span class=\"fn\"><a href=\"./Init/Core.html#Task\">Task</a> <span class=\"fn\">α</span></span>)</span></span> <span class=\"decl_args\"><span class=\"fn\">(<span class=\"fn\">timeout</span> : <a href=\"./Std/Time/Time/Unit/Millisecond.html#Std.Time.Millisecond.Offset\">Time.Millisecond.Offset</a>)</span></span> <span class=\"decl_args\"> :</span><div class=\"decl_type\"><span class=\"fn\"><a href=\"./Init/System/IO.html#BaseIO\">BaseIO</a> <a href=\"./Init/Prelude.html#Unit\">Unit</a></span></div></div>","info":{"doc":"Starts a wait that must end within `timeout` of `task` finishing, and that does not time out before\nthen: a deadline set for the current wait is dropped. If the wait ends, or is armed again, before\n`task` finishes, nothing is armed. Does nothing once the watchdog has fired.","docLink":"./Std/Async/Watchdog.html#Std.Async.Watchdog.armAfter","kind":"def","line":174,"name":"Std.Async.Watchdog.armAfter","sourceLink":"https://github.com/leanprover/lean4/blob/0b77e12952ad39077d80d8bd6b66d601f225c321/src/Std/Async/Watchdog.lean#L174-L185"}},{"header":"<div class=\"decl_header\"><span class=\"decl_kind\">def</span><span class=\"decl_name\"> <a class=\"break_within\" href=\"./Std/Async/Watchdog.html#Std.Async.Watchdog.armUntil\"><span class=\"name\">Std</span>.<span class=\"name\">Async</span>.<span class=\"name\">Watchdog</span>.<span class=\"name\">armUntil</span></a> </span><span class=\"decl_args\"><span class=\"fn\">(<span class=\"fn\">wd</span> : <a href=\"./Std/Async/Watchdog.html#Std.Async.Watchdog\">Watchdog</a>)</span></span> <span class=\"decl_args\"><span class=\"fn\">(<span class=\"fn\">deadline</span> : <a href=\"./Init/Prelude.html#Nat\">Nat</a>)</span></span> <span class=\"decl_args\"> :</span><div class=\"decl_type\"><span class=\"fn\"><a href=\"./Init/System/IO.html#BaseIO\">BaseIO</a> <a href=\"./Init/Prelude.html#Unit\">Unit</a></span></div></div>","info":{"doc":"Starts a wait that must end by `deadline`, a value of `IO.monoMsNow`. Arming again before `disarm`\nreplaces the deadline. Does nothing once the watchdog has fired.","docLink":"./Std/Async/Watchdog.html#Std.Async.Watchdog.armUntil","kind":"def","line":167,"name":"Std.Async.Watchdog.armUntil","sourceLink":"https://github.com/leanprover/lean4/blob/0b77e12952ad39077d80d8bd6b66d601f225c321/src/Std/Async/Watchdog.lean#L167-L172"}},{"header":"<div class=\"decl_header\"><span class=\"decl_kind\">def</span><span class=\"decl_name\"> <a class=\"break_within\" href=\"./Std/Async/Watchdog.html#Std.Async.Watchdog.new\"><span class=\"name\">Std</span>.<span class=\"name\">Async</span>.<span class=\"name\">Watchdog</span>.<span class=\"name\">new</span></a> </span><span class=\"decl_args\"><span class=\"fn\">(<span class=\"fn\">ctx</span> : <a href=\"./Std/Sync/CancellationContext.html#Std.CancellationContext\">CancellationContext</a>)</span></span> <span class=\"decl_args\"> :</span><div class=\"decl_type\"><span class=\"fn\"><a href=\"./Init/System/IO.html#IO\">IO</a> <a href=\"./Std/Async/Watchdog.html#Std.Async.Watchdog\">Watchdog</a></span></div></div>","info":{"doc":"Creates a watchdog that cancels `ctx` with `.deadline` when a wait outlives its deadline.\n\nThe watchdog and its timer stay alive until `ctx` is cancelled, so `ctx` should be cancelled once\nthe watchdog is no longer needed.","docLink":"./Std/Async/Watchdog.html#Std.Async.Watchdog.new","kind":"def","line":135,"name":"Std.Async.Watchdog.new","sourceLink":"https://github.com/leanprover/lean4/blob/0b77e12952ad39077d80d8bd6b66d601f225c321/src/Std/Async/Watchdog.lean#L135-L150"}},{"header":"<div class=\"decl_header\"><span class=\"decl_kind\">structure</span><span class=\"decl_name\"> <a class=\"break_within\" href=\"./Std/Async/Watchdog.html#Std.Async.Watchdog\"><span class=\"name\">Std</span>.<span class=\"name\">Async</span>.<span class=\"name\">Watchdog</span></a> </span><span class=\"decl_args\"> :</span><div class=\"decl_type\"><a href=\"./foundational_types.html\">Type</a></div></div>","info":{"doc":"Enforces deadlines on a sequence of waits with a single background timer. A wait starts with\n`arm` and ends with `disarm`; when one outlives its deadline, the watchdog cancels its context with\n`.deadline` and stops. The context is never cancelled before the deadline.\n\nWaits whose deadlines keep moving later, such as idle timeouts, cost no timer operation each: only\na deadline earlier than the one the timer is set for restarts it.\n\nThe context is cancelled from a task on the shared task pool, so while every worker is busy, a late\nwait may stay uncancelled until one is free. `disarm` reports a late wait regardless.\n\nThe watchdog and its timer stay alive until the context is cancelled, so the context should be\ncancelled once the watchdog is no longer needed.","docLink":"./Std/Async/Watchdog.html#Std.Async.Watchdog","kind":"structure","line":68,"name":"Std.Async.Watchdog","sourceLink":"https://github.com/leanprover/lean4/blob/0b77e12952ad39077d80d8bd6b66d601f225c321/src/Std/Async/Watchdog.lean#L68-L93"}}],"imports":["Std.Internal.UV.Timer","Std.Sync.CancellationContext","Std.Time"],"instances":[],"name":"Std.Async.Watchdog"}